{"id":"G2228","lemma":"ἤ","transliteration":"ē","sayIt":"ē","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"or","meaning":"ἤ,\ndisjunctive and comparative particle (Bl., §36, 12; 77, 11);\n1. disjunctive, or;\n(a) between single words: Mat.5:17 Mrk.6:56, Luk.2:24, Jhn.6:19, Rom.1:21, al.;\n(b) before a sentence expressing a variation, denial or refutation of a previous statement, frequently in interrog. form: Mat.7:4, 9 Mrk.12:14, Luk.13:4, Rom.3:29 6:3 9:21, 1Co.6:9, 16 9:6, 2Co.11:7; ἤ . . . ἤ, either . . . or, Mat.6:24, Luk.16:13, 1Co.14:6;\n(with) in a disjunctive question (as Lat. an after utrum): Mat.9:5, Mrk.2:9, Luk.7:19, al.; after πότερον, Jhn.7:17; μή, 1Co.9:8; μήτι, 2Co.1:17; ἤ . . . ἤ . . . ἤ, Mrk.13:35.\n2. Comparative, than: after comparatives, Mat.10:15, Luk.9:13, Jhn.3:19, Rom.13:11, al.; after ἕτερον, Act.17:21; θέλω (Khüner 3, iv, 303), 1Co.14:19; πρὶν ἤ, before, before accusative and inf., Mat.1:18 Mrk.14:30; after a positive adj. (Gen.49:12; cf. Robertson, Gr., 661), Mat.18:8, 9 Mrk.9:43, 45 47.\n3. with other particles: ἀλλ᾽ ἤ, see: ἀλλά; ἤ γάρ, see: γάρ; ἢ καί, or even, or also, Mat.7:10, Luk.11:11, 12 Rom.2:15 4:9, al; ἤτοι . . . ἤ, Rom.6:16 (cf. Wis.11:19).\n(AS)","glosses":["or","than","and","than for","but","either"],"count":275,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":18,"renderings":{"bsb":"but","kjv":"before"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":17,"renderings":{"bsb":"or","kjv":"or"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":18,"renderings":{"bsb":"not","kjv":"or"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":36,"renderings":{"bsb":"or","kjv":"or"}},{"chapterId":"mat-6","v":24,"renderings":{"bsb":"Either","kjv":"either"}},{"chapterId":"mat-6","v":25,"renderings":{}},{"chapterId":"mat-6","v":31,"renderings":{"bsb":"or","kjv":"or"}},{"chapterId":"mat-7","v":4,"renderings":{"kjv":"Or"}},{"chapterId":"mat-7","v":9,"renderings":{"kjv":"Or"}},{"chapterId":"mat-7","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"Or"}},{"chapterId":"mat-7","v":16,"renderings":{"bsb":"or","kjv":"or"}},{"chapterId":"mat-9","v":5,